      "content": [
        "Hebrews"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "1",
      "sid": "HEB 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Supremacy of the Son"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "COL 1:15-23",
          "content": [
            "Colossians 1:15–23"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "HEB 1:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "On many"
          ]
        },
        " past occasions and in many different ways, God spoke to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " fathers through the prophets. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "HEB 1:2"
        },
        "But in these last days He has spoken to us by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " Son,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "in His Son"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " whom He appointed heir of all things, and through whom He made the universe.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the world"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the ages"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "HEB 1:3"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The Son"
          ]
        },
        " is ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " radiance of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God’s"
          ]
        },
        " glory and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " exact representation of His nature, upholding all things by His powerful word. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "After"
          ]
        },
        " He had provided purification for sins, He sat down at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " right hand of the Majesty on high. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "HEB 1:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " He became as far superior to the angels as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " name He has inherited ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " excellent beyond theirs. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "HEB 1:5"
        },
        "For to which of the angels did ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " ever say:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“You are My Son;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "today I have become Your Father”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 2:7",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 2:7"
                  ]
                },
                "; literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "today I have begotten You"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Or"
          ]
        },
        " again:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“I will be His Father,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and He will be My Son”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "2SA 7:14",
                  "content": [
                    "2 Samuel 7:14"
                  ]
                },
                "; 1 Chronicles 17:13"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "HEB 1:6"
        },
        "And again, when ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " brings ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " firstborn into the world, He says:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Let"
          ]
        },
        " all God’s angels worship Him.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "DEU 32:43",
                  "content": [
                    "Deuteronomy 32:43"
                  ]
                },
                " (see DSS and LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "HEB 1:7"
        },
        "Now about the angels He says:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“He makes His angels winds,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "His servants flames of fire.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:7 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 104:4",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 104:4"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "HEB 1:8"
        },
        "But about the Son ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He says"
          ]
        },
        ":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“Your throne, O God, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "endures"
          ]
        },
        " forever and ever,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and justice ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " the scepter of Your kingdom."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "HEB 1:9"
        },
        "You have loved righteousness"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and hated wickedness;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "therefore God, Your God, has anointed You"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "above Your companions with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " oil of joy.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:9 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 45:6-7",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 45:6–7"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "HEB 1:10"
        },
        "And:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“In ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " beginning, O Lord, You laid the foundations of the earth,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and the heavens are ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " work of Your hands."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "HEB 1:11"
        },
        "They will perish, but You remain;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "they will all wear out like a garment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "HEB 1:12"
        },
        "You will roll them up like a robe;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "like a garment",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR do not include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "like a garment"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " they will be changed;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "but You remain the same,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and Your years will never end.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 102:25-27",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 102:25–27"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "HEB 1:13"
        },
        "Yet to which of the angels did ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " ever say:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“Sit at My right hand"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "until I make Your enemies a footstool for Your feet”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:13 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 110:1",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 110:1"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "HEB 1:14"
        },
        "Are not ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the angels"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "1:14 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Are they not all"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " ministering spirits sent to serve those who will inherit salvation?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "2",
      "sid": "HEB 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Salvation Confirmed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "HEB 2:1"
        },
        "We must pay closer attention, therefore, to what we have heard, so that we do not drift away. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "HEB 2:2"
        },
        "For if the message spoken by angels was binding, and every transgression and disobedience received ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "its"
          ]
        },
        " just punishment, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "HEB 2:3"
        },
        "how shall we escape if we neglect such a great salvation?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "This salvation "
          ]
        },
        " was first announced by the Lord, was confirmed to us by those who heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "HEB 2:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " was affirmed by God through signs, wonders, various miracles, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "gifts"
          ]
        },
        " of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit distributed according to His will."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus like His Brothers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "HEB 2:5"
        },
        "For ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it is"
          ]
        },
        " not to angels that He has subjected the world to come, about which we are speaking. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "HEB 2:6"
        },
        "But somewhere it is testified in these words:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“What is man that You are mindful of him,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "or ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " son of man that You care for him?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "HEB 2:7"
        },
        "You made him a little lower",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:7 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "a little while lower"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verse 9"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " than ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " angels;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "You crowned him with glory and honor",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:7 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "WH and TR include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "and set him over the works of Your hands"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "HEB 2:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " placed everything under his feet.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:8 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 8:4-6",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 8:4–6"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When God"
          ]
        },
        " subjected all things to him, He left nothing outside of his control. Yet at present we do not see everything subject to him. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "HEB 2:9"
        },
        "But we see Jesus, who was made a little lower than ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " angels, now crowned with glory and honor because He suffered death, so that by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " grace of God He might taste death for everyone."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "HEB 2:10"
        },
        "In bringing many sons to glory, it was fitting for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        ", for whom and through whom all things ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "exist"
          ]
        },
        ", to make the author",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:10 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "pioneer "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "founder"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " of their salvation ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "perfect"
          ]
        },
        " through suffering. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "HEB 2:11"
        },
        "For both the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One who"
          ]
        },
        " sanctifies and those who are sanctified ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " of the same ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "family"
          ]
        },
        ". So ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " is not ashamed to call them brothers. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "HEB 2:12"
        },
        "He says:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“I will proclaim Your name to My brothers;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "I will sing Your praises in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " assembly.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 22:22",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 22:22"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "HEB 2:13"
        },
        "And again:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“I will put ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "My"
          ]
        },
        " trust in Him.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:13 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ISA 8:17",
                  "content": [
                    "Isaiah 8:17"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "once"
          ]
        },
        " again:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“Here ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "am"
          ]
        },
        " I, and the children God has given Me.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:13 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ISA 8:18",
                  "content": [
                    "Isaiah 8:18"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "HEB 2:14"
        },
        "Now since the children have flesh and blood, He too shared in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "humanity"
          ]
        },
        ", so that by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " death He might destroy him who holds the power of death, that is, the devil, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "HEB 2:15"
        },
        "and free those who all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " lives were held in slavery by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " fear of death."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "HEB 2:16"
        },
        "For surely ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it is"
          ]
        },
        " not ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " angels He helps, but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " descendants of Abraham. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "HEB 2:17"
        },
        "For this reason He had to be made like ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " brothers in every way, so that He might become a merciful and faithful high priest ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in service"
          ]
        },
        " to God, in order to make atonement",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "2:17 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "to make propitiation"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " for the sins of the people. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "HEB 2:18"
        },
        "Because He Himself suffered when He was tempted, He is able to help those who are being tempted."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "3",
      "sid": "HEB 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Jesus Our Apostle and High Priest"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "HEB 3:1"
        },
        "Therefore, holy brothers, who share in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " heavenly calling, set your focus on Jesus, the apostle and high priest whom we confess. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "HEB 3:2"
        },
        "He was faithful to the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One who"
          ]
        },
        " appointed Him, just as Moses ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was faithful"
          ]
        },
        " in all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God’s"
          ]
        },
        " house.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "just as Moses in all His house"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; SBL "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "just as Moses in His house"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "HEB 3:3"
        },
        "For ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " has been counted worthy of greater glory than Moses, just as the builder ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of a house"
          ]
        },
        " has greater honor than the house ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "itself"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "HEB 3:4"
        },
        "And every house is built by someone, but God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " the builder of everything."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "HEB 3:5"
        },
        "Now Moses ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " faithful as a servant in all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God’s"
          ]
        },
        " house,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "NUM 12:7",
                  "content": [
                    "Numbers 12:7"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " testifying to what would be spoken later. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "HEB 3:6"
        },
        "But Christ ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is faithful"
          ]
        },
        " as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Son over ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God’s"
          ]
        },
        " house. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "And"
          ]
        },
        " we are ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " house, if we hold firmly",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "NE, WH, BYZ, and TR include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "to the end"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " confidence and the hope ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of which"
          ]
        },
        " we boast."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Do Not Harden Your Hearts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "PSA 95:1-11",
          "content": [
            "Psalm 95:1–11"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "HEB 3:7"
        },
        "Therefore, as the Holy Spirit says:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“Today, if you hear His voice,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "HEB 3:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do"
          ]
        },
        " not harden your hearts,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you did"
          ]
        },
        " in the rebellion,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "in the day of testing in the wilderness,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "HEB 3:9"
        },
        "where your fathers tested ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " tried ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Me"
          ]
        },
        ","
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and for forty years saw My works."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "HEB 3:10"
        },
        "Therefore I was angry with that generation,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and I said,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "‘Their hearts ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " always going astray,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and they have not known My ways.’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "HEB 3:11"
        },
        "So I swore on oath in My anger,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "‘They shall never enter My rest.’”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:11 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 95:7-11",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 95:7–11"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Peril of Unbelief"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "HEB 3:12"
        },
        "See to it, brothers, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "none"
          ]
        },
        " of you has a wicked heart of unbelief that turns away from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " living God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "HEB 3:13"
        },
        "But exhort one another daily, as long as it is called today, so that none of you may be hardened by sin’s deceitfulness."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "HEB 3:14"
        },
        "We have come to share in Christ if we hold firmly to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " end the assurance ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "we had"
          ]
        },
        " at first. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "HEB 3:15"
        },
        "As it has been said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“Today, if you hear His voice,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do"
          ]
        },
        " not harden your hearts,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "you did"
          ]
        },
        " in the rebellion.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "3:15 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 95:7-8",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 95:7–8"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "HEB 3:16"
        },
        "For who were the ones who heard ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " rebelled? ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Were they"
          ]
        },
        " not all those Moses led out of Egypt? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "HEB 3:17"
        },
        "And with whom was ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " angry for forty years? ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Was it"
          ]
        },
        " not with those who sinned, whose bodies fell in the wilderness? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "HEB 3:18"
        },
        "And to whom did He swear ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that they"
          ]
        },
        " would never enter His rest? ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Was it"
          ]
        },
        " not to those who disobeyed? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "HEB 3:19"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "So"
          ]
        },
        " we see that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it was"
          ]
        },
        " because of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " unbelief that they were unable to enter."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "4",
      "sid": "HEB 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Sabbath Rest"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "GEN 2:1-3",
          "content": [
            "Genesis 2:1–3"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 16:22-30",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 16:22–30"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "HEB 4:1"
        },
        "Therefore,  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "while "
          ]
        },
        " the promise of entering His rest still stands, let us be careful that none of you be deemed to have fallen short ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of it"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "HEB 4:2"
        },
        "For we also received the good news just as they ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "did"
          ]
        },
        "; but the message they heard was of no value to them, since they did not share the faith of those who comprehended ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ".",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "not having been united in the faith of those who heard"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "HEB 4:3"
        },
        "Now ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "we"
          ]
        },
        " who have believed enter ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " rest. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "As for the others, "
          ]
        },
        " it is just as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " has said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“So I swore on oath in My anger,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "‘They shall never enter My rest.’”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:3 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 95:11",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 95:11"
                  ]
                },
                "; also in verse 5"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "And yet ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " works have been finished since ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " foundation of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " world. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "HEB 4:4"
        },
        "For somewhere He has spoken about the seventh ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "day"
          ]
        },
        " in this manner: “And on the seventh day God rested from all His works.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:4 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "GEN 2:2",
                  "content": [
                    "Genesis 2:2"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "HEB 4:5"
        },
        "And again, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as He says"
          ]
        },
        " in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the passage above"
          ]
        },
        ": “They shall never enter My rest.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "HEB 4:6"
        },
        "Since, then, it remains ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        " some to enter ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His rest"
          ]
        },
        ", and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "since"
          ]
        },
        " those who formerly heard the good news did not enter because of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " disobedience, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "HEB 4:7"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " again designated a certain day ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as"
          ]
        },
        " “Today,” when a long time later He spoke through David as was just stated: “Today, if you hear His voice, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do"
          ]
        },
        " not harden your hearts.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "4:7 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 95:7-8",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 95:7–8"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "HEB 4:8"
        },
        "For if Joshua had given them rest, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " would not have spoken later about another day. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "HEB 4:9"
        },
        "There remains, then, a Sabbath rest for the people of God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "HEB 4:10"
        },
        "For whoever enters ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God’s"
          ]
        },
        " rest also rests from his ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "own"
          ]
        },
        " work, just as God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "did"
          ]
        },
        " from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "HEB 4:11"
        },
        "Let us, therefore, make every effort to enter that rest, so that no one will fall by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "following"
          ]
        },
        " the same pattern of disobedience."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Living Word"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "2TI 3:10-17",
          "content": [
            "2 Timothy 3:10–17"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "HEB 4:12"
        },
        "For the word of God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " living and active. Sharper than any double-edged sword, it pierces even to dividing soul and spirit, joints and marrow. It judges ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " thoughts and intentions of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " heart. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "HEB 4:13"
        },
        "Nothing in all creation is hidden from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God’s"
          ]
        },
        " sight; everything ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " uncovered and exposed before the eyes of Him to whom we ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "must give"
          ]
        },
        " account."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "HEB 4:14"
        },
        "Therefore, since we have a great high priest who has passed through the heavens, Jesus the Son of God, let us hold firmly to what we profess. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "HEB 4:15"
        },
        "For we do not have a high priest who is unable to sympathize with our weaknesses, but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "we have"
          ]
        },
        " one who was tempted in every way that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "we are"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "yet was"
          ]
        },
        " without sin. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "HEB 4:16"
        },
        "Let us then approach the throne of grace with confidence, so that we may receive mercy and find grace to help ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "us"
          ]
        },
        " in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " time of need."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "5",
      "sid": "HEB 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Perfect High Priest"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "PSA 110:1-7",
          "content": [
            "Psalm 110:1–7"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "HEB 5:1"
        },
        "Every high priest is appointed from among men to represent ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " in matters relating to God, to offer gifts and sacrifices for sins. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "HEB 5:2"
        },
        "He is able to deal gently with those who are ignorant and misguided, since he himself is subject to weakness. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "HEB 5:3"
        },
        "That is why he is obligated to offer sacrifices for his own sins, as well as for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the sins of"
          ]
        },
        " the people."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "HEB 5:4"
        },
        "No one takes ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " honor upon himself; he must be called by God, just as Aaron ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "HEB 5:5"
        },
        "So also Christ ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "did"
          ]
        },
        " not take upon Himself the glory of becoming a high priest, but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He was called"
          ]
        },
        " by the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One who"
          ]
        },
        " said to Him:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“You are My Son;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "today I have become Your Father.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 2:7",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 2:7"
                  ]
                },
                "; literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "today I have begotten You"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "HEB 5:6"
        },
        "And in another ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "passage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " says:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“You ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " a priest forever"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "in the order of Melchizedek.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 110:4",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 110:4"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "HEB 5:7"
        },
        "During the days of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus’"
          ]
        },
        " earthly ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "life"
          ]
        },
        ", He offered up prayers and petitions with loud cries and tears to the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One who"
          ]
        },
        " could save Him from death, and He was heard because of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " reverence. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "HEB 5:8"
        },
        "Although He was a Son, He learned obedience from what He suffered. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "HEB 5:9"
        },
        "And having been made perfect, He became ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " source of eternal salvation to all who obey Him ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "HEB 5:10"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " was designated by God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as"
          ]
        },
        " high priest in the order of Melchizedek."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Milk and Solid Food"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "1CO 3:1-9",
          "content": [
            "1 Corinthians 3:1–9"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "HEB 5:11"
        },
        "We ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "have"
          ]
        },
        " much to say about ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but it is"
          ]
        },
        " hard to explain, because you are dull of hearing. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "HEB 5:12"
        },
        "Although by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " time you ought to be teachers, you need ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "someone"
          ]
        },
        " to reteach you the basic principles of God’s word.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "5:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "of the oracles of God"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " You need milk, not solid food!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "HEB 5:13"
        },
        "For everyone who lives on milk is ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "still"
          ]
        },
        " an infant, inexperienced in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " message of righteousness. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "HEB 5:14"
        },
        "But solid food is ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for the"
          ]
        },
        " mature, who by constant use have trained ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " senses to distinguish good ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "from"
          ]
        },
        " evil."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "6",
      "sid": "HEB 6"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Call to Maturity"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "HEB 6:1"
        },
        "Therefore let us leave the elementary teachings about Christ ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " go on to maturity, not laying again ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " foundation of repentance from dead works,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "6:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "from acts that lead to death"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and of faith in God, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "HEB 6:2"
        },
        "instruction about baptisms,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "6:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "cleansing rites"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " laying on of hands, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " resurrection of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead, and eternal judgment. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "HEB 6:3"
        },
        "And this we will do, if God permits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "HEB 6:4"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It is"
          ]
        },
        " impossible for those who have once been enlightened, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " have tasted the heavenly gift, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " have shared in ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Spirit, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "HEB 6:5"
        },
        "who have tasted ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " goodness ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of the"
          ]
        },
        " word of God and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " powers ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of the"
          ]
        },
        " coming age — ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "HEB 6:6"
        },
        "and then have fallen away — to be restored to repentance, because they themselves are crucifying the Son of God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "all over again"
          ]
        },
        " and subjecting ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " to open shame."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "HEB 6:7"
        },
        "For land that drinks in the rain often falling on it and that produces a crop useful to those for whom it is tended receives ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " blessing of God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "HEB 6:8"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "land that"
          ]
        },
        " produces thorns and thistles ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " worthless, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "its"
          ]
        },
        " curse is imminent. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "In"
          ]
        },
        " the end it will be burned."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "HEB 6:9"
        },
        "Even though we speak like this, beloved, we are convinced of better ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "things"
          ]
        },
        " in your ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "case"
          ]
        },
        "— ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "things that"
          ]
        },
        " accompany salvation. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "HEB 6:10"
        },
        "For God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " not unjust. He will not forget your work and the love you have shown for His name as you have ministered to the saints and continue to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do so"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "HEB 6:11"
        },
        "We want each of you to show ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this"
          ]
        },
        " same diligence to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the very"
          ]
        },
        " end, in order ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to make"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your"
          ]
        },
        " hope sure. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "HEB 6:12"
        },
        "Then you will not be sluggish, but will imitate those who through faith and patience inherit what has been promised."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "God’s Unchangeable Promise"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "HEB 6:13"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " God made His promise to Abraham, since He had no one greater to swear by, He swore by Himself, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "HEB 6:14"
        },
        "saying, “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "I will"
          ]
        },
        " surely bless you and multiply your ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "descendants"
          ]
        },
        ".”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "6:14 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "GEN 22:17",
                  "content": [
                    "Genesis 22:17"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "HEB 6:15"
        },
        "And so ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Abraham"
          ]
        },
        ", after waiting patiently, obtained the promise."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "HEB 6:16"
        },
        "Men swear by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "someone"
          ]
        },
        " greater ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "than themselves"
          ]
        },
        ", and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " oath serves as a confirmation to end all argument. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "HEB 6:17"
        },
        "So when God wanted to make the unchanging nature of His purpose very clear to the heirs of the promise, He guaranteed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " with an oath. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "HEB 6:18"
        },
        "Thus by two unchangeable things in which ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it is"
          ]
        },
        " impossible ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        " God to lie, we who have fled to take hold of the hope set before ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "us"
          ]
        },
        " may be strongly encouraged."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "HEB 6:19"
        },
        "We have ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this hope"
          ]
        },
        " as an anchor for the soul, firm and secure. It enters the inner ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "sanctuary"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "behind"
          ]
        },
        " the curtain, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "HEB 6:20"
        },
        "where Jesus ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " forerunner has entered on our behalf. He has become a high priest forever in the order of Melchizedek."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "7",
      "sid": "HEB 7"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Melchizedek and Abraham"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "GEN 14:17-24",
          "content": [
            "Genesis 14:17–24"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "HEB 7:1"
        },
        "This Melchizedek ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " king of Salem ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " priest of God Most High.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "GEN 14:18",
                  "content": [
                    "Genesis 14:18"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " He met Abraham returning from the slaughter of the kings and blessed him, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "HEB 7:2"
        },
        "and Abraham apportioned to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " a tenth of everything. First, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his name"
          ]
        },
        " means “king of righteousness.” Then also, “king of Salem” means “king of peace.” ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "HEB 7:3"
        },
        "Without father ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " mother ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " genealogy, without beginning of days ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " end of life, like the Son of God, he remains a priest for all time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "HEB 7:4"
        },
        "Consider how great ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Melchizedek was"
          ]
        },
        ": Even the patriarch Abraham gave ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        " a tenth of the plunder. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "HEB 7:5"
        },
        "Now the law commands the sons of Levi who become priests to collect a tenth from the people — that is, from their brothers — though they ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "too"
          ]
        },
        " are descended from Abraham. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "HEB 7:6"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Melchizedek"
          ]
        },
        ", who did not trace his descent from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Levi"
          ]
        },
        ", collected a tenth from Abraham and blessed him who had the promises. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "HEB 7:7"
        },
        "And indisputably, the lesser is blessed by the greater."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "HEB 7:8"
        },
        "In the case ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of the Levites"
          ]
        },
        ", mortal men collect the tenth; but in the case ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of Melchizedek"
          ]
        },
        ", it is affirmed that he lives on. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "HEB 7:9"
        },
        "And so to speak, Levi, who collects ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " tenth, paid ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " tenth through Abraham. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "HEB 7:10"
        },
        "For when Melchizedek met Abraham, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Levi"
          ]
        },
        " was still in the loin of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " ancestor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Superior Priesthood"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "HEB 7:11"
        },
        "Now if perfection could have been attained through the Levitical priesthood (for on this basis the people received ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " law), why ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was there"
          ]
        },
        " still need ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        " another priest to appear — ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one"
          ]
        },
        " in the order of Melchizedek and not in the order of Aaron? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "HEB 7:12"
        },
        "For ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " the priesthood is changed, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " law must be changed as well."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "HEB 7:13"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " of whom these things are said belonged to a different tribe, from which no one has ever served at the altar. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "HEB 7:14"
        },
        "For ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it is"
          ]
        },
        " clear that our Lord descended from Judah, a tribe as to which Moses said nothing about priests."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "HEB 7:15"
        },
        "And  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "this point "
          ]
        },
        " is even more clear if another priest like Melchizedek appears, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "HEB 7:16"
        },
        "one who has become ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a priest"
          ]
        },
        " not by a law of succession, but by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " power of an indestructible life. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "HEB 7:17"
        },
        "For it is testified:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“You ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " a priest forever"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "in the order of Melchizedek.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:17 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 110:4",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 110:4"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "HEB 7:18"
        },
        "So the former commandment is set aside because it ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " weak and useless ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "HEB 7:19"
        },
        "(for the law made nothing perfect), and a better hope ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " introduced, by which we draw near to God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "HEB 7:20"
        },
        "And none of this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "happened"
          ]
        },
        " without an oath. For ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "others"
          ]
        },
        " became priests without an oath, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "HEB 7:21"
        },
        "but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus became a priest"
          ]
        },
        " with an oath by the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One who"
          ]
        },
        " said to Him:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The"
          ]
        },
        " Lord has sworn and will not change His mind:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "‘You ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " a priest forever.’”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 110:4",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 110:4"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "HEB 7:22"
        },
        "Because of this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "oath"
          ]
        },
        ", Jesus has become ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " guarantee of a better covenant."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "HEB 7:23"
        },
        "Now there have been many ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "other"
          ]
        },
        " priests, since death prevented them from continuing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "in office"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "HEB 7:24"
        },
        "But because ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " lives forever, He has a permanent priesthood. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "HEB 7:25"
        },
        "Therefore He is able to save completely",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "7:25 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "forever"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " those who draw near to God through Him, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "since He"
          ]
        },
        " always lives to intercede for them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "HEB 7:26"
        },
        "Such a high priest truly befits us — ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "One who is"
          ]
        },
        " holy, innocent, undefiled, set apart from sinners, and exalted above the heavens. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "HEB 7:27"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Unlike"
          ]
        },
        " the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "other"
          ]
        },
        " high priests, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He"
          ]
        },
        " does not need to offer daily sacrifices, first for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " own sins and then for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the sins"
          ]
        },
        " of the people; He ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "sacrificed for sin"
          ]
        },
        " once for all when He offered up Himself. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "HEB 7:28"
        },
        "For the law appoints as high priests men who are weak; but the oath, which ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "came"
          ]
        },
        " after the law, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "appointed"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Son, who has been made perfect forever."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "8",
      "sid": "HEB 8"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Christ’s Eternal Priesthood"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "HEB 8:1"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The"
          ]
        },
        " point of what we are saying ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is this"
          ]
        },
        ": We do have such a high priest, who sat down at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " right hand of the throne of the Majesty in heaven, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "HEB 8:2"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and who"
          ]
        },
        " ministers in the sanctuary and true tabernacle set up by the Lord, not by man. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "HEB 8:3"
        },
        "And since every high priest is appointed to offer both gifts and sacrifices, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it was"
          ]
        },
        " necessary ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        " this One also to have something to offer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "HEB 8:4"
        },
        "Now if He were on earth, He would not be a priest, since there are already ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "priests"
          ]
        },
        " who offer gifts according to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " law. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "HEB 8:5"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The place where"
          ]
        },
        " they serve ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " a copy and shadow of what is in heaven. This is why Moses was warned when he was about to build the tabernacle: “See to it that you make everything according to the pattern shown you on the mountain.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "8:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 25:40",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 25:40"
                  ]
                },
                "; see also Exodus 26:30."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The New Covenant"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JER 31:26-40",
          "content": [
            "Jeremiah 31:26–40"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "HEB 8:6"
        },
        "Now, however, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        " has received a much more excellent ministry, just as the covenant He mediates is better ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " is founded on better promises. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "HEB 8:7"
        },
        "For if that first  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "covenant "
          ]
        },
        " had been without fault, no place would have been sought for a second. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "HEB 8:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "But"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " found fault with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“Behold, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " days are coming, declares ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " I will make a new covenant"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "with the house of Israel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and with the house of Judah."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "HEB 8:9"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It will"
          ]
        },
        " not be like the covenant"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "I made with their fathers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "when I took them by the hand"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "to lead them out of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " land of Egypt,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "because they did not abide by My covenant,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and I disregarded them,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "qr",
      "content": [
        "declares ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "HEB 8:10"
        },
        "For this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " the covenant I will make"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "with the house of Israel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "after those days,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "declares ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "I will put My laws in their minds"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and inscribe them on their hearts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "And I will be their God,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and they will be My people."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "HEB 8:11"
        },
        "No longer ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "will"
          ]
        },
        " each one teach his neighbor ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " his brother,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "saying, ‘Know the Lord,’"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "because they will all know Me,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " least of them to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " greatest."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "HEB 8:12"
        },
        "For I will forgive their iniquities"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and will remember their sins no more.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "8:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "JER 31:31-34",
                  "content": [
                    "Jeremiah 31:31–34"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "HEB 8:13"
        },
        "By speaking of a new ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "covenant"
          ]
        },
        ",",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "8:13 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "In saying new"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; here and in ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "HEB 9:1",
                  "content": [
                    "Hebrews 9:1"
                  ]
                },
                " and 18, "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "covenant "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "is included for clarity but is not contained in the Greek. A broader interpretation could also include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "priesthood "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "tabernacle"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " He has made the first one ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "obsolete"
          ]
        },
        "; and what is obsolete and aging will soon disappear."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "9",
      "sid": "HEB 9"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Earthly Tabernacle"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 40:1-33",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 40:1–33"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 7:44-47",
          "content": [
            "Acts 7:44–47"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "HEB 9:1"
        },
        "Now the first  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "covenant "
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:1 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the first"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verse 18; see the footnote for ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "HEB 8:13",
                  "content": [
                    "Hebrews 8:13"
                  ]
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " had regulations for worship and also an earthly sanctuary. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "HEB 9:2"
        },
        "A tabernacle was prepared. In ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "its"
          ]
        },
        " first ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "room"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "were"
          ]
        },
        " the lampstand, the table, and the consecrated bread.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Bread of the Presence"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " This was called ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Holy ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Place"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "HEB 9:3"
        },
        "Behind the second curtain ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " a room called ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Most Holy Place,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:3 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Holy of Holies"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "HEB 9:4"
        },
        "containing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " golden altar of incense and the gold-covered ark of the covenant. Inside ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the ark"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "were the"
          ]
        },
        " gold jar of manna, Aaron’s staff that had budded, and the stone tablets of the covenant. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "HEB 9:5"
        },
        "Above ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the ark"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "were the"
          ]
        },
        " cherubim of glory, overshadowing the mercy seat.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "atonement cover"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "But"
          ]
        },
        " we cannot discuss ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "these things"
          ]
        },
        " in detail now."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "HEB 9:6"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "When"
          ]
        },
        " everything had been prepared in this way, the priests entered regularly into the first room to perform ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " sacred duties. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "HEB 9:7"
        },
        "But only the high priest ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "entered"
          ]
        },
        " the second ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "room"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and then"
          ]
        },
        " only once a year, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " never without blood, which he offered for himself and for the sins the people had committed in ignorance."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "HEB 9:8"
        },
        "By this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "arrangement"
          ]
        },
        " the Holy Spirit was showing ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " the way into the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Most"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Place",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:8 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Holy Place"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; also in verses 12 and 25"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "had"
          ]
        },
        " not yet been disclosed ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as long as"
          ]
        },
        " the first tabernacle was still standing. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "HEB 9:9"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It is"
          ]
        },
        " an illustration for the present time, because ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " gifts and sacrifices being offered were unable to cleanse ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " conscience of the worshiper. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "HEB 9:10"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "They consist "
          ]
        },
        " only in food and drink and special washings — external regulations imposed until ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " time of reform."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Redemption through His Blood"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "HEB 9:11"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " Christ came as high priest of the good things that have come,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:11 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "that are to come"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He went through"
          ]
        },
        " the greater and more perfect tabernacle that is not made by hands ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and is"
          ]
        },
        " not ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a part"
          ]
        },
        " of this creation. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "HEB 9:12"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He did not enter"
          ]
        },
        " by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " blood of goats and calves, but He entered the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Most"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Place once for all by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " own blood, thus securing eternal redemption."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "HEB 9:13"
        },
        "For if the blood of goats and bulls and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " ashes of a heifer sprinkled on those who are ceremonially unclean sanctify ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " so that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " bodies are clean, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "HEB 9:14"
        },
        "how much more ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "will"
          ]
        },
        " the blood of Christ, who through ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " eternal Spirit offered Himself unblemished to God, purify our",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:14 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "your"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " consciences from works of death, so that we may serve ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " living God!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "HEB 9:15"
        },
        "Therefore ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Christ"
          ]
        },
        " is ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " mediator of a new covenant, so that those who are called may receive the promised eternal inheritance, now that He has died to redeem ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " from the transgressions ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "committed"
          ]
        },
        " under the first covenant."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "HEB 9:16"
        },
        "In the case of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a"
          ]
        },
        " will,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Greek "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "diathēkē "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "is also translated as "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "covenant "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "throughout this chapter."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it is"
          ]
        },
        " necessary to establish ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " death of the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one who"
          ]
        },
        " made ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "HEB 9:17"
        },
        "because a will ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "does not"
          ]
        },
        " take effect until the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one who"
          ]
        },
        " made ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " has died; it cannot be executed while he is still alive."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "HEB 9:18"
        },
        "That is why ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "even"
          ]
        },
        " the first ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "covenant"
          ]
        },
        " was not put into effect without blood. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "HEB 9:19"
        },
        "For ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " Moses had proclaimed every commandment of the law to all the people, he took the blood of calves and goats,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:19 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "SBL does not include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "and goats"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " along with water, scarlet wool, and hyssop, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " sprinkled the scroll and all the people, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "HEB 9:20"
        },
        "saying, “This ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " the blood of the covenant, which God has commanded you ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to keep"
          ]
        },
        ".”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "9:20 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 24:8",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 24:8"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "HEB 9:21"
        },
        "In the same way, he sprinkled with blood the tabernacle and all the vessels used in worship. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "HEB 9:22"
        },
        "According to the law, in fact, nearly everything must be purified with blood, and without the shedding of blood there is no forgiveness."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "HEB 9:23"
        },
        "So ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it was"
          ]
        },
        " necessary ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        " the copies ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of"
          ]
        },
        " the heavenly things to be purified with these ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "sacrifices"
          ]
        },
        ", but the heavenly things themselves with better sacrifices than these. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "HEB 9:24"
        },
        "For Christ did not enter a man-made copy of the true sanctuary, but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "He entered"
          ]
        },
        " heaven itself, now to appear on our behalf in the presence of God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "HEB 9:25"
        },
        "Nor ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "did He enter heaven"
          ]
        },
        " to offer Himself again and again, as the high priest enters the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Most"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Place every year with blood that is not his own. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "HEB 9:26"
        },
        "Otherwise, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Christ"
          ]
        },
        " would have had to suffer repeatedly since ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " foundation of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " world. But now He has appeared once ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for all"
          ]
        },
        " at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " end of the ages to do away with sin by the sacrifice of Himself."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "HEB 9:27"
        },
        "Just as man is appointed to die once, and after that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to face"
          ]
        },
        " judgment, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "HEB 9:28"
        },
        "so also Christ was offered once to bear ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " sins of many; ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " He will appear a second time, not to bear sin, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        " to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "bring"
          ]
        },
        " salvation to those who eagerly await Him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "10",
      "sid": "HEB 10"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Christ’s Perfect Sacrifice"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "PSA 40:1-17",
          "content": [
            "Psalm 40:1–17"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "HEB 10:1"
        },
        "For the law is only a shadow of the good things to come, not the realities themselves. It can never, by the same sacrifices offered year after year, make perfect those who draw near  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to worship "
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "HEB 10:2"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "If it could"
          ]
        },
        ", would not the offerings have ceased? For the worshipers would have been cleansed once ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for all"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " would no longer have felt the guilt of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " sins."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "HEB 10:3"
        },
        "Instead, those ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "sacrifices"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "are"
          ]
        },
        " an annual reminder of sins, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "HEB 10:4"
        },
        "because ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it is"
          ]
        },
        " impossible ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "for the"
          ]
        },
        " blood of bulls and goats to take away sins. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "HEB 10:5"
        },
        "Therefore, when ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Christ"
          ]
        },
        " came into the world, He said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Sacrifice and offering You did not desire,"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "but a body You prepared for Me."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "HEB 10:6"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "In burnt offerings and sin ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "offerings"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "You took no delight."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "HEB 10:7"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "Then I said, ‘Here I am, it is written about Me in ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "the"
              ]
            },
            " scroll:"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "I have come to do Your will, O God.’”",
            {
              "type": "note",
              "marker": "f",
              "caller": "+",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "fr",
                  "content": [
                    "10:7 "
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "char",
                  "marker": "ft",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "ref",
                      "loc": "PSA 40:6-8",
                      "content": [
                        "Psalm 40:6–8"
                      ]
                    },
                    " (see also LXX)"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "HEB 10:8"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "In the passage "
          ]
        },
        " above He says, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Sacrifices and offerings, burnt offerings and sin ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "offerings"
              ]
            },
            " You did not desire, nor did You delight in ",
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "add",
              "content": [
                "them"
              ]
            },
            "”"
          ]
        },
        " (",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "although"
          ]
        },
        " they are offered according to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " law). ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "HEB 10:9"
        },
        "Then He adds, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "wj",
          "content": [
            "“Here I am, I have come to do Your will.”"
          ]
        },
        " He takes away the first to establish the second. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "HEB 10:10"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "And"
          ]
        },
        " by that will, we have been sanctified through the sacrifice of the body of Jesus Christ once for all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "HEB 10:11"
        },
        "Day after day every priest stands to minister and to offer again and again the same sacrifices, which can never take away sins. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "HEB 10:12"
        },
        "But ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " this ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Priest"
          ]
        },
        " had offered for all time one sacrifice for sins, He sat down at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " right hand of God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "HEB 10:13"
        },
        "Since that time, He waits for His enemies to be made a footstool for His feet, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "HEB 10:14"
        },
        "because by a single offering He has made perfect for all time those who are being sanctified."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "HEB 10:15"
        },
        "The Holy Spirit also testifies to us ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "about this"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "First"
          ]
        },
        " He says:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "HEB 10:16"
        },
        "“This ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " the covenant I will make with them"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "after those days, declares ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "I will put My laws in their hearts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and inscribe them on their minds.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:16 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "JER 31:33",
                  "content": [
                    "Jeremiah 31:33"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "HEB 10:17"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Then He adds"
          ]
        },
        ":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“Their sins and lawless acts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "I will remember no more.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:17 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "JER 31:34",
                  "content": [
                    "Jeremiah 31:34"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "HEB 10:18"
        },
        "And where these have been forgiven, an offering for sin ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " no longer ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "needed "
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Call to Persevere"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JUD 17-23",
          "content": [
            "Jude 1:17–23"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "HEB 10:19"
        },
        "Therefore, brothers, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "since"
          ]
        },
        " we have confidence to enter the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Most"
          ]
        },
        " Holy Place",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:19 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "the Holy Place"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " by the blood of Jesus, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "HEB 10:20"
        },
        "by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " new and living way opened for us through the curtain of His body,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:20 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "through the veil that is His flesh"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "HEB 10:21"
        },
        "and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "since we have"
          ]
        },
        " a great priest over the house of God, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "HEB 10:22"
        },
        "let us draw near with a sincere heart in full assurance of faith, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "having"
          ]
        },
        " our hearts sprinkled to cleanse us from a guilty conscience and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " bodies washed with pure water."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "HEB 10:23"
        },
        "Let us hold resolutely to the hope we profess, for He who promised ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " faithful. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "HEB 10:24"
        },
        "And let us consider how to spur one another ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "on"
          ]
        },
        " to love and good deeds. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "HEB 10:25"
        },
        "Let us not neglect meeting together, as some ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "have made a"
          ]
        },
        " habit, but let us encourage ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one another"
          ]
        },
        ", and all ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " more as you see the Day approaching."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "HEB 10:26"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "If"
          ]
        },
        " we deliberately go on sinning after we have received the knowledge of the truth, no further sacrifice for sins remains, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "HEB 10:27"
        },
        "but only a fearful expectation of judgment and of raging fire that will consume ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "all"
          ]
        },
        " adversaries. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "HEB 10:28"
        },
        "Anyone who rejected ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " law of Moses died without mercy on ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the testimony of"
          ]
        },
        " two or three witnesses. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "HEB 10:29"
        },
        "How much more severely do you think one deserves to be punished ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " has trampled on the Son of God, profaned the blood of the covenant that sanctified him, and insulted the Spirit of grace?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "HEB 10:30"
        },
        "For we know Him who said, “Vengeance ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " Mine; I will repay,”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:30 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "DEU 32:35",
                  "content": [
                    "Deuteronomy 32:35"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and again, “",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The"
          ]
        },
        " Lord will judge His people.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:30 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "DEU 32:36",
                  "content": [
                    "Deuteronomy 32:36"
                  ]
                },
                "; Psalm 135:14"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "HEB 10:31"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "It is"
          ]
        },
        " a fearful thing to fall into ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " hands of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " living God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "HEB 10:32"
        },
        "Remember the early days that you were in the light.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:32 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Remember when you were first enlightened."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " In ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "those days"
          ]
        },
        ", you endured a great conflict in the face of suffering. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "HEB 10:33"
        },
        "Sometimes you were publicly exposed to ridicule and persecution; at other times you were partners with those who ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "were"
          ]
        },
        " so treated. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "HEB 10:34"
        },
        "You sympathized with those in prison and joyfully accepted the confiscation of your property, knowing that you yourselves had a better and permanent possession."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "HEB 10:35"
        },
        "So ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do"
          ]
        },
        " not throw away your confidence; ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it"
          ]
        },
        " holds a great reward. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "HEB 10:36"
        },
        "You need to persevere, so that after you have done the will of God, you will receive what He has promised. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "HEB 10:37"
        },
        "For,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“In just a little while,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "He who is coming will come and will not delay."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "HEB 10:38"
        },
        "But My righteous one will live by faith;",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:38 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "But the righteous will live by faith"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and if he shrinks back,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "I ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "will take"
          ]
        },
        " no pleasure in him.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "10:38 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "HAB 2:3-4",
                  "content": [
                    "Habakkuk 2:3–4"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "HEB 10:39"
        },
        "But we are not of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "those who"
          ]
        },
        " shrink back ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " are destroyed, but of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "those who have"
          ]
        },
        " faith ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " preserve ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " souls."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "11",
      "sid": "HEB 11"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Faith and Assurance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "GEN 1:1-2",
          "content": [
            "Genesis 1:1–2"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "JHN 1:1-5",
          "content": [
            "John 1:1–5"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "HEB 11:1"
        },
        "Now faith is ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " assurance of what ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "we"
          ]
        },
        " hope for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and the"
          ]
        },
        " certainty of what we do not see. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "HEB 11:2"
        },
        "This is why the ancients were commended."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "HEB 11:3"
        },
        "By faith we understand that the universe was formed at God’s command, so that what is seen was not made out of what was visible."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Faith of Abel, Enoch, Noah"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "content": [
            "Genesis 4–9"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "HEB 11:4"
        },
        "By faith Abel offered God a better sacrifice than Cain ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "did"
          ]
        },
        ". By ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "faith"
          ]
        },
        " he was commended as righteous ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " God gave approval to his gifts. And by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "faith"
          ]
        },
        " he still speaks, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "even though"
          ]
        },
        " he is dead."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "HEB 11:5"
        },
        "By faith Enoch was taken up",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "11:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "transferred "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "translated"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "so that"
          ]
        },
        " he did not see death: “He could not be found, because God had taken him away.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "11:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "GEN 5:24",
                  "content": [
                    "Genesis 5:24"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " For before he was taken, he was commended as one who pleased God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "HEB 11:6"
        },
        "And without faith ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it is"
          ]
        },
        " impossible to please ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        ". For anyone who approaches ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him"
          ]
        },
        " must believe that He exists and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " He rewards those who earnestly seek Him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "HEB 11:7"
        },
        "By faith Noah, when warned about things not yet seen, in godly fear built an ark to save his family. By ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "faith"
          ]
        },
        " he condemned the world and became heir of the righteousness ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " comes by faith."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Faith of Abraham and Sarah"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "content": [
            "Genesis 15–22"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ROM 4:1-12",
          "content": [
            "Romans 4:1–12"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "HEB 11:8"
        },
        "By faith Abraham, when called to go to a place he would later receive as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " inheritance, obeyed and went, without knowing where he was going. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "HEB 11:9"
        },
        "By faith he dwelt in the promised land as ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a stranger"
          ]
        },
        " in a foreign ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "country"
          ]
        },
        ". He lived in tents, as did Isaac and Jacob, who ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "were"
          ]
        },
        " heirs with him of the same promise. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "HEB 11:10"
        },
        "For he was looking forward to the city with foundations, whose architect and builder ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " God."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "HEB 11:11"
        },
        "By faith Sarah, even though she was barren and beyond the proper age, was enabled to conceive a child, because she considered Him faithful who had promised. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "HEB 11:12"
        },
        "And so from one man, and he as good as dead, came descendants as numerous as the stars in the sky and as countless as the sand on the seashore."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "HEB 11:13"
        },
        "All these ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " died in faith, without having received the things they were promised. However, they saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " and welcomed them from afar. And they acknowledged that they were strangers and exiles on the earth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "HEB 11:14"
        },
        "Now those who say such things show that they are seeking a country of their own. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "HEB 11:15"
        },
        "If they had been thinking of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the country"
          ]
        },
        " they had left, they would have had opportunity to return. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "HEB 11:16"
        },
        "Instead, they were longing for a better ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "country"
          ]
        },
        ", a heavenly ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "one"
          ]
        },
        ". Therefore God is not ashamed to be called their God, for He has prepared a city for them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "HEB 11:17"
        },
        "By faith Abraham, when he was tested, offered up Isaac  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "on the altar "
          ]
        },
        ". He who had received the promises was ready to offer ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " one and only son,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "11:17 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "only begotten son "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "unique son"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "HEB 11:18"
        },
        "even though ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " had said to him, “Through Isaac your offspring will be reckoned.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "11:18 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "GEN 21:12",
                  "content": [
                    "Genesis 21:12"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "HEB 11:19"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Abraham"
          ]
        },
        " reasoned that God could raise ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " in a sense, he did receive ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Isaac"
          ]
        },
        " back from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "death"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Faith of Isaac, Jacob, and Joseph"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "content": [
            "Genesis 27–50"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "HEB 11:20"
        },
        "By faith Isaac blessed Jacob and Esau concerning the future."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "HEB 11:21"
        },
        "By faith Jacob, when he was dying, blessed each of Joseph’s sons and worshiped ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as he leaned"
          ]
        },
        " on the top of his staff."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "HEB 11:22"
        },
        "By faith Joseph, when his end was near, spoke about the exodus of the Israelites and gave instructions about his bones."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Faith of Moses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 2–15"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "ACT 7:20-22",
          "content": [
            "Acts 7:20–22"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "HEB 11:23"
        },
        "By faith ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Moses’"
          ]
        },
        " parents hid him for three months after his birth, because they saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that he was"
          ]
        },
        " a beautiful child, and they were unafraid of the king’s edict."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "HEB 11:24"
        },
        "By faith Moses, when he was grown, refused to be called ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " son of Pharaoh’s daughter. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "HEB 11:25"
        },
        "He chose to suffer oppression with God’s people rather than to experience ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " fleeting enjoyment of sin. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "HEB 11:26"
        },
        "He valued disgrace for Christ ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "above"
          ]
        },
        " the treasures of Egypt, for he was looking ahead to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "his"
          ]
        },
        " reward."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "HEB 11:27"
        },
        "By faith ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Moses"
          ]
        },
        " left Egypt, not fearing the king’s anger; he persevered because he saw ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Him who is"
          ]
        },
        " invisible. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "HEB 11:28"
        },
        "By faith he kept the Passover and the sprinkling of blood, so that the destroyer ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of"
          ]
        },
        " the firstborn would not touch ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Israel’s own"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "firstborn "
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "HEB 11:29"
        },
        "By faith ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        " passed through the Red Sea as on dry land; ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "but when"
          ]
        },
        " the Egyptians tried to follow,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "11:29 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "made an attempt"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " they were drowned."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "The Faith of Many"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "30",
          "sid": "HEB 11:30"
        },
        "By faith the walls of Jericho fell, after ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        " had marched around them for seven days."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "31",
          "sid": "HEB 11:31"
        },
        "By faith the prostitute Rahab, because she welcomed the spies in peace, did not perish with those who were disobedient."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "32",
          "sid": "HEB 11:32"
        },
        "And what more shall I say? Time will not allow me to tell of Gideon, Barak, Samson, Jephthah, David, Samuel, and the prophets, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "33",
          "sid": "HEB 11:33"
        },
        "who through faith conquered kingdoms, administered justice, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " gained what was promised; ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " shut ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " mouths of lions, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "34",
          "sid": "HEB 11:34"
        },
        "quenched ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " raging fire, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " escaped ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " edge of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " sword; ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "who"
          ]
        },
        " gained strength from weakness, became mighty in battle, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " put foreign armies ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to flight"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "35",
          "sid": "HEB 11:35"
        },
        "Women received back their dead, raised to life again. Others were tortured ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " refused ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " release, so that they might gain a better resurrection. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "36",
          "sid": "HEB 11:36"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Still"
          ]
        },
        " others endured mocking and flogging, and even chains and imprisonment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "37",
          "sid": "HEB 11:37"
        },
        "They were stoned, they were sawed in two,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "11:37 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "NE, WH, BYZ, and TR include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "they were put to the test,"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " they were put to death by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " sword. They went around in sheepskins ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " goatskins, destitute, oppressed, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " mistreated. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "38",
          "sid": "HEB 11:38"
        },
        "The world was not worthy of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ". They wandered in deserts and mountains, and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "hid in "
          ]
        },
        " caves and holes in the ground."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "39",
          "sid": "HEB 11:39"
        },
        "These ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "were"
          ]
        },
        " all commended for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " faith, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "yet"
          ]
        },
        " they did not receive what ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "was"
          ]
        },
        " promised. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "40",
          "sid": "HEB 11:40"
        },
        "God had planned something better for us, so that together with us they would be made perfect."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "12",
      "sid": "HEB 12"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Call to Endurance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "2TI 2:1-13",
          "content": [
            "2 Timothy 2:1–13"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "HEB 12:1"
        },
        "Therefore, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "since"
          ]
        },
        " we are surrounded by such a great cloud of witnesses, let us throw off every encumbrance and the sin ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " so easily entangles, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " let us run with endurance the race set out for us. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "HEB 12:2"
        },
        "Let us fix our eyes on Jesus, the author",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "12:2 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "pioneer "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "founder"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " and perfecter of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " faith, who for the joy set before Him endured ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " cross, scorning ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "its"
          ]
        },
        " shame, and sat down at ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " right hand of the throne of God. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "HEB 12:3"
        },
        "Consider Him who endured such hostility from sinners, so that you will not grow weary ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " lose heart."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "God Disciplines His Sons"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "HEB 12:4"
        },
        "In your struggle against sin, you have not yet resisted to the point of shedding your blood. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "HEB 12:5"
        },
        "And you have forgotten the exhortation that addresses you as sons:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“My son, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do"
          ]
        },
        " not take lightly ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " discipline of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do not"
          ]
        },
        " lose heart ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "when"
          ]
        },
        " He rebukes you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "HEB 12:6"
        },
        "For ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Lord disciplines the one He loves,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "and He chastises every son He receives.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "12:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "and He flogs every son He receives"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "; ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PRO 3:11-12",
                  "content": [
                    "Proverbs 3:11–12"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "HEB 12:7"
        },
        "Endure suffering as discipline; God is treating you as sons. For what son is not disciplined ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "by his"
          ]
        },
        " father? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "HEB 12:8"
        },
        "If you do not experience discipline like everyone else, then you are illegitimate children and not true sons. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "HEB 12:9"
        },
        "Furthermore, we have all had earthly fathers who disciplined ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "us"
          ]
        },
        ", and we respected ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Should we"
          ]
        },
        " not much more submit to the Father of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " spirits and live?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "HEB 12:10"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Our fathers"
          ]
        },
        " disciplined ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "us"
          ]
        },
        " for a short time as they thought best, but ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God disciplines us"
          ]
        },
        " for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "our"
          ]
        },
        " good, so that we may share in His holiness. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "HEB 12:11"
        },
        "No discipline seems enjoyable at the time, but painful. Later on, however, it yields a harvest of righteousness ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " peace",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "12:11 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Or "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "it yields the peaceful fruit of righteousness"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to those who have been trained by it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "HEB 12:12"
        },
        "Therefore strengthen ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "your"
          ]
        },
        " limp hands and weak knees.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "12:12 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "ISA 35:3",
                  "content": [
                    "Isaiah 35:3"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "HEB 12:13"
        },
        "Make straight paths for your feet,",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "12:13 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PRO 4:26",
                  "content": [
                    "Proverbs 4:26"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " so that the lame ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "may"
          ]
        },
        " not be disabled, but rather healed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "A Call to Holiness"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "1PE 1:13-21",
          "content": [
            "1 Peter 1:13–21"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "HEB 12:14"
        },
        "Pursue peace with everyone, as well as holiness, without which no one will see the Lord. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "HEB 12:15"
        },
        "See to it that no one falls short of the grace of God, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " that no root of bitterness",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "12:15 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "See ",
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "DEU 29:18",
                  "content": [
                    "Deuteronomy 29:18"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " springs up to cause trouble and defile many. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "HEB 12:16"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "See to it"
          ]
        },
        " that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "no one is"
          ]
        },
        " sexually immoral, or is godless like Esau, who for a single meal sold his birthright. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "HEB 12:17"
        },
        "For you know that afterward, when he wanted to inherit the blessing, he was rejected. He could find no ground for repentance, though he sought ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the blessing"
          ]
        },
        " with tears."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "An Unshakable Kingdom"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "r",
      "content": [
        "(",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "EXO 20:18-21",
          "content": [
            "Exodus 20:18–21"
          ]
        },
        "; ",
        {
          "type": "ref",
          "loc": "DEU 5:22-33",
          "content": [
            "Deuteronomy 5:22–33"
          ]
        },
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "HEB 12:18"
        },
        "For you have not come to  ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a mountain that "
          ]
        },
        " can be touched and ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "12:18 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "Literally "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "to what can be touched and"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " is burning with fire; to darkness, gloom, and storm; ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "HEB 12:19"
        },
        "to a trumpet blast ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "or"
          ]
        },
        " to a voice that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "made"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "its"
          ]
        },
        " hearers beg that no further word be spoken. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "HEB 12:20"
        },
        "For they could not bear what was commanded: “If even an animal touches the mountain, it must be stoned.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "12:20 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "EXO 19:12-13",
                  "content": [
                    "Exodus 19:12–13"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "HEB 12:21"
        },
        "The sight was so terrifying ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " even Moses said, “I am trembling with fear.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "12:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "DEU 9:19",
                  "content": [
                    "Deuteronomy 9:19"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "HEB 12:22"
        },
        "Instead, you have come to Mount Zion, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to the"
          ]
        },
        " city of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " living God, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " heavenly Jerusalem. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "You have come"
          ]
        },
        " to myriads of angels ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "HEB 12:23"
        },
        "in joyful assembly, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to the"
          ]
        },
        " congregation of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " firstborn, enrolled in heaven. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "You have come"
          ]
        },
        " to God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " Judge of all, to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " spirits of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " righteous made perfect, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "HEB 12:24"
        },
        "to Jesus ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " mediator of a new covenant, and to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " sprinkled blood that speaks a better word than ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the blood"
          ]
        },
        " of Abel."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "HEB 12:25"
        },
        "See to it that you do not refuse Him who speaks. For if ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the people"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "did"
          ]
        },
        " not escape when they refused Him who warned ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        " on earth, how much less ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "will"
          ]
        },
        " we ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "escape"
          ]
        },
        " if we reject Him who ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "warns us"
          ]
        },
        " from heaven? ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "26",
          "sid": "HEB 12:26"
        },
        "At that time ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " voice shook the earth, but now He has promised, “Once more I will shake not only the earth, but heaven as well.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "12:26 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "HAG 2:6",
                  "content": [
                    "Haggai 2:6"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "27",
          "sid": "HEB 12:27"
        },
        "The ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "words"
          ]
        },
        " “Once more” signify the removal of what can be shaken — that is, created things — so that the unshakable may remain."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "28",
          "sid": "HEB 12:28"
        },
        "Therefore, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "since"
          ]
        },
        " we are receiving an unshakable kingdom, let us be filled with gratitude, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and so"
          ]
        },
        " worship God acceptably with reverence and awe. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "29",
          "sid": "HEB 12:29"
        },
        "“For our God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is a"
          ]
        },
        " consuming fire.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "12:29 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "DEU 4:24",
                  "content": [
                    "Deuteronomy 4:24"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "marker": "c",
      "number": "13",
      "sid": "HEB 13"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Brotherly Love"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "1",
          "sid": "HEB 13:1"
        },
        "Continue in brotherly love. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "2",
          "sid": "HEB 13:2"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Do"
          ]
        },
        " not neglect to show hospitality to strangers, for by so doing some ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "people"
          ]
        },
        " have entertained angels without knowing it. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "3",
          "sid": "HEB 13:3"
        },
        "Remember those in prison as if you were bound with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ", ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " those who are mistreated as if you were ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "suffering with them"
          ]
        },
        "."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "4",
          "sid": "HEB 13:4"
        },
        "Marriage should be honored by all and the marriage bed kept undefiled, for God will judge the sexually immoral and adulterers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Christ’s Unchanging Nature"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "5",
          "sid": "HEB 13:5"
        },
        "Keep your lives free from the love of money ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " be content with what you have, for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "God"
          ]
        },
        " has said:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“Never will I leave you,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "never will I forsake you.”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "13:5 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "DEU 31:6",
                  "content": [
                    "Deuteronomy 31:6"
                  ]
                },
                ", 8; Joshua 1:5"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "6",
          "sid": "HEB 13:6"
        },
        "So we say with confidence:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "b"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q1",
      "content": [
        "“",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "The"
          ]
        },
        " Lord ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " my helper; I will not be afraid."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "q2",
      "content": [
        "What ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "can"
          ]
        },
        " man do to me?”",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "13:6 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "loc": "PSA 118:6",
                  "content": [
                    "Psalm 118:6"
                  ]
                },
                " (see also LXX)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "7",
          "sid": "HEB 13:7"
        },
        "Remember your leaders who spoke the word of God to you. Consider the outcome of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " way of life ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " imitate ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "their"
          ]
        },
        " faith. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "8",
          "sid": "HEB 13:8"
        },
        "Jesus Christ ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " the same yesterday and today and forever."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "9",
          "sid": "HEB 13:9"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Do"
          ]
        },
        " not be carried away ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "by"
          ]
        },
        " all kinds ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "of"
          ]
        },
        " strange teachings, for ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "it is"
          ]
        },
        " good for the heart to be strengthened by grace ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " not by foods of no value to those devoted to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "them"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "10",
          "sid": "HEB 13:10"
        },
        "We have an altar from which those who serve at the tabernacle have no right to eat."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "11",
          "sid": "HEB 13:11"
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Although"
          ]
        },
        " the high priest brings the blood of animals into the Holy Place ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "as a sacrifice"
          ]
        },
        " for sin, the bodies are burned outside the camp. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "12",
          "sid": "HEB 13:12"
        },
        "And so Jesus ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "also"
          ]
        },
        " suffered outside the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "city"
          ]
        },
        " gate, to sanctify the people by ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "His"
          ]
        },
        " own blood. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "13",
          "sid": "HEB 13:13"
        },
        "Therefore let us go to Him outside the camp, bearing the disgrace He ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "bore"
          ]
        },
        ". ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "14",
          "sid": "HEB 13:14"
        },
        "For here we do not have a permanent city, but we are looking for the ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "city"
          ]
        },
        " that is to come."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Sacrifice, Obedience, and Prayer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "15",
          "sid": "HEB 13:15"
        },
        "Through ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "Jesus"
          ]
        },
        ", therefore, let us continually offer to God ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "a"
          ]
        },
        " sacrifice of praise, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " fruit of lips that confess His name. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "16",
          "sid": "HEB 13:16"
        },
        "And ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "do"
          ]
        },
        " not neglect to do good and to share with others, for with such sacrifices God is pleased."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "17",
          "sid": "HEB 13:17"
        },
        "Obey your leaders and submit ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to them"
          ]
        },
        ", for they watch over your souls as those who must give an account. To this end, allow them ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to lead"
          ]
        },
        " with joy and not ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "with"
          ]
        },
        " grief, for that ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "would be"
          ]
        },
        " of no advantage to you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "18",
          "sid": "HEB 13:18"
        },
        "Pray for us; we are convinced that we have a clear conscience ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " desire to live honorably in every way. ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "19",
          "sid": "HEB 13:19"
        },
        "And I especially urge you to ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "pray"
          ]
        },
        " that I may be restored to you soon."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "s1",
      "content": [
        "Benediction and Farewell"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "20",
          "sid": "HEB 13:20"
        },
        "Now ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "may"
          ]
        },
        " the God of peace, who through ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " blood of ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " eternal covenant brought back from ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "the"
          ]
        },
        " dead our Lord Jesus, ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " great Shepherd of the sheep, ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "21",
          "sid": "HEB 13:21"
        },
        "equip you with every good ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "thing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "13:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "every good work"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " to do His will. ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "And"
          ]
        },
        " may He accomplish in us",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "13:21 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "you"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        " what ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "is"
          ]
        },
        " pleasing in His sight through Jesus Christ, to whom ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "be"
          ]
        },
        " glory forever ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "and"
          ]
        },
        " ever. Amen."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "22",
          "sid": "HEB 13:22"
        },
        "I urge you, brothers, to bear with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "my"
          ]
        },
        " word of exhortation, for I have ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "only"
          ]
        },
        " written to you briefly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "23",
          "sid": "HEB 13:23"
        },
        "Be aware ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "that"
          ]
        },
        " our brother Timothy has been released. If he arrives soon, I will come with ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "him"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "to see"
          ]
        },
        " you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "24",
          "sid": "HEB 13:24"
        },
        "Greet all your leaders and all the saints."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        "Those from Italy send you greetings."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "marker": "p",
      "content": [
        " ",
        {
          "type": "verse",
          "marker": "v",
          "number": "25",
          "sid": "HEB 13:25"
        },
        "Grace ",
        {
          "type": "char",
          "marker": "add",
          "content": [
            "be"
          ]
        },
        " with all of you.",
        {
          "type": "note",
          "marker": "f",
          "caller": "+",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fr",
              "content": [
                "13:25 "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "ft",
              "content": [
                "BYZ and TR include "
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "char",
              "marker": "fqa",
              "content": [
                "Amen."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}